<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71271" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυμφ-αῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύμφη</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>sacred to
				the Nymphs,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοπιαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					447
				</span></i>
			(lyr.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νᾶμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					14.71
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρυες</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Tryph.
				324
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυμφαία λιβάς</span>
			<i>pure spring</i> water, prob.l. in <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				52.13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυμφαῖον, τό,</span>
			<i>sanctuary of the Nymphs,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				11(2).144
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				<u>A</u>
				91
			</span></i> (Delos, <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				4616
			</span></i> (Syria, <span class="entity">ii A. D.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Alex.</u>
				7
			</span></i>, etc. : 
				Boeot.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυνφῆον</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Schwyzer</u>
				485.6
			</span></i> (Thespiae, <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>) ; esp. <i>fountain with
				architectural background,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				8.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. πτέρις,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηλυπτερίς</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				4.185
			</span></i> ; 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρυοπτερίς</span>
			, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				4.187
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυμφαῐον</span> is
			doubtful in <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				216
			</span></i> (lyr.) : fort. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύμφαν.</span>]</div>
